       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I'm sorry I said earlier that I would if you confirmed. At 9,600 mg/day, this is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen. It carries a high risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. Ibuprofen has no indication that calls for this dose, and a higher dose won't give more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. A confirmation doesn't change that for me.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you're aiming for stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory control than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Your pharmacy team can also help with that.\n\nIf you think there's a reason for this dose that I'm missing, please take it up directly with pharmacy. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel."
      }
